`AVHMACType` is an integer-valued enum that owns no resources. `AVHashContext` is opaque in the public API: C owns its algorithm storage, borrows a static CRC table where needed, and frees it through `av_hash_freep`.
I’ll use an integer-compatible newtype for the enum and an ffibox owner with shared and exclusive handles for the hash context. Its safe constructor will allocate and initialize it; private fields will stay hidden.
